[00:27.74] [I. Prelude]
[02:59.12] When our weary world was young
[03:01.82] The struggle of the ancients first began.
[03:06.48] The gods of Love and Reason
[03:09.52] Sought alone to rule the fate of Man.
[03:19.96] They battled through the ages,
[03:23.46] But still neither force would yield.
[03:26.76] The people were divided,
[03:29.82] Every soul a battlefield.
[04:10.10] [II. Apollo: Bringer of Wisdom]
[04:36.38] "I bring truth and understanding,
[04:39.34] I bring wit and wisdom fair,
[04:42.10] Precious gifts beyond compare.
[04:52.34] We can build a world of wonder,
[04:55.90] I can make you all aware.
[04:59.18] I will find you food and shelter,
[05:02.18] Show you fire to keep you warm
[05:05.20] Through the endless winter storm.
[05:15.96] You can live in grace and comfort
[05:18.80] In the world that you transform."
[05:38.74] The people were delighted
[05:41.24] Coming forth to claim their prize
[05:45.02] They ran to build their cities
[05:49.18] And converse among the wise.
[05:52.72] But one day the streets fell silent,
[05:55.76] Yet they knew not what was wrong.
[06:00.12] The urge to build these fine things
[06:03.32] Seemed not to be so strong.
[06:06.96] The wise men were consulted,
[06:09.56] And the Bridge of Death was crossed
[06:12.78] In quest of Dionysus,
[06:17.80] To find out what they had lost.
[06:22.08] [III. Dionysus: Bringer of Love]
[06:36.14] "I bring love to give you solace
[06:38.30] In the darkness of the night,
[07:11.90] In the Heart's eternal light.
[07:21.86] You need only trust your feelings;
[07:25.50] Only love can steer you right.
[07:28.92] I bring laughter, I bring music,
[07:31.68] I bring joy and I bring tears.
[07:35.00] I will soothe your primal fears.
[07:45.76] Throw off those chains of reason
[07:48.66] And your prison disappears."
[08:08.50] The cities were abandoned,
[08:11.20] And the forests echoed song.
[08:14.78] They danced and lived as brothers;
[08:18.96] They knew love could not be wrong.
[08:22.76] Food and wine they had aplenty
[08:25.22] And they slept beneath the stars.
[08:29.96] The people were contented
[08:33.32] And the Gods watched from afar.
[08:36.96] But the winter fell upon them
[08:40.06] And it caught them unprepared,
[08:44.32] Bringing wolves and cold starvation,
[08:47.72] And the hearts of men despaired.
[08:52.24] [IV. Armageddon: The Battle of Heart and Mind]
[09:53.55] The Universe divided
[09:55.47] As the Heart and Mind collided,
[09:57.55] With the people left unguided
[09:59.89] For so many troubled years.
[10:02.17] In a cloud of doubts and fears,
[10:04.03] Their world was torn asunder into hollow Hemispheres.
[10:20.85] Some fought themselves, some fought each other.
[10:23.19] Most just followed one another,
[10:25.25] Lost and aimless like their brothers,
[10:27.49] For their hearts were so unclear,
[10:29.47] And the truth could not appear.
[10:31.17] Their spirits were divided into blinded Hemispheres.
[10:56.57] Some who did not fight
[10:58.93] Brought tales of old to light.
[11:03.37] My Rocinante' sailed by night
[11:07.97] On her final flight.
[11:12.15] To the heart of Cygnus' fearsome force
[11:16.13] We set our course.
[11:20.89] Spiralled through that timeless space
[11:24.49] To this immortal place.
[11:50.33] [V. Cygnus: Bringer of Balance]
[11:50.41] I have memory and awareness,
[11:54.81] But I have no shape or form.
[12:54.29] As a disembodied spirit,
[12:57.13] I am dead and yet unborn.
[13:04.01] I have passed into Olympus
[13:07.65] As was told in tales of old,
[13:12.19] To the city of Immortals,
[13:16.43] Marble white and purest gold.
[14:06.39] I see the gods in battle rage on high
[14:13.99] Thunderbolts across the sky.
[14:19.71] I cannot move, I cannot hide,
[14:24.75] I feel a silent scream begin inside.
[14:35.81] Then all at once the chaos ceased.
[14:39.07] A stillness fell, a sudden peace.
[14:42.35] The warriors felt my silent cry
[14:45.77] And stayed their struggle, mystified.
[14:52.89] Apollo was astonished;
[14:55.83] Dionysus thought me mad.
[15:00.19] But they heard my story further,
[15:03.17] And they wondered, and were sad.
[15:07.77] Looking down from Olympus
[15:10.25] On a world of doubt and fear,
[15:15.53] Its surface splintered
[15:18.29] Into sorry Hemispheres.
[15:37.83] They sat a while in silence,
[15:40.67] Then they turned at last to me.
[15:44.63] "We will call you Cygnus,
[15:47.57] The god of Balance you shall be."
[15:52.79] [VI. The Sphere: A Kind of Dream]
[17:02.59] We can walk our road together
[17:08.11] If our goals are all the same.
[17:13.75] We can run alone and free
[17:18.87] If we pursue a different aim.
[17:24.87] Let the truth of love be lighted,
[17:30.39] Let the love of truth shine clear.
[17:35.39] Sensibility, armed with sense and liberty,
[17:40.95] With the Heart and Mind united in a single perfect Sphere.
